      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "For anyone using `dev-mode` locally (`--preset dev-mode)`, the `32.x`, `31.x` and `30.x` branches will currently fail to configure if CMake >= 4.5.0 is used. The value of catching CMake dev warnings/errors on those branches seems limited, so remove it for now. This will also effect the CI for those branches, if a newer CMake begins being used, i.e in the macOS or Windows jobs.\n\nAn alternative would be to backport a secp256k1 subtree update to all those branches. I'm not sure we want to do that, so just disable turning the warnings into errors (and a subtree pull could happen regardless).\n\nFollowup to https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/36913#issuecomment-7007283917.",
